"""Long-form article — Best Roof Racks & Crossbars for 2023–2026 Toyota Sequoia (3rd gen, XK80, hybrid only).
Mirrors the approved pilot (ford_f150_2021_tonneau.py) and the roof-rack guides (4Runner 2025, Tahoe 2021, Highlander
2020). No invented hands-on testing. Vehicle facts: db/migrations/003_vehicles.sql; etrailer's 2023 and 2024 Sequoia
roof pages (two roof types, "Factory installed raised rails that run front to back" and "Flush mounted rails that run
front to back", no grades named, only Front Runner platforms shown, "Factory roof rails will be removed prior to
installation"); Rack Warehouse (Thule Evo Raised Rail rack for the 2001–2025 Sequoia, 165 lb, $444.90; Yakima
TimberLine FX for the 2001–2025 Sequoia, $599.90; Sequoia category page with raised-rail systems and Prinsu platforms
for 2023–2026, no flush-rail system); Rave Offroad (TRD Pro factory roof rack, 132 lb evenly distributed, 67.5 in
long, $989 sale / $1,350 regular); Toyota Newsroom releases for the 2023 reveal (five grades, 9,000 lb) and the 2025
model year (six grades, 9,520 lb; neither describes the roof rails); Wikipedia (GA-F platform, XK80, i-FORCE MAX);
Dometic (Front Runner Slimsport KSTS003T: $1,249, 105 x 54.4 in load area, 5-year warranty) and OK4WD (same kit,
103.6 lb, 2023–2024). All opened 2026-10-05. Amazon picks are identified by listing title read in amazon.com search
results; amazon.com pages cannot be fetched, so each pick says which specs come from the title only. No Toyota roof
load figure was read; the page says so and sends readers to the owner's manual. No Thule, Yakima or Rhino-Rack
listing naming the 2023+ Sequoia was found on amazon.com, so those systems are described from Rack Warehouse and are
not picks. Toyota's PT767-0C660 bars (B0C26KKRF3) and the ROSY PIXEL bars (B0DJZZLPPT) already belong to the cargo
box guide's FITS and are not repeated here.
"""

