FAQ = [
 ("What is the best roof rack for a 2023–2026 Toyota Sequoia?",
  "The Tuyoung 260 lb lockable crossbars are the best overall pick. The title names the 2023–2026 Sequoia, prints a 260 lb rating and says lockable, the only set here with both. The ANTS PART bars are the budget pick and run 2023 through 2026 by title. The Front Runner Slimsport KSTS003T is the premium platform for an overland build, with a 105 x 54.4 in deck, though OK4WD lists it at 103.6 lb before cargo. If you want a 165 lb rating in writing, Rack Warehouse sells a Thule or Yakima raised-rail kit through a dealer. Look under the rail first: etrailer lists both raised and flush rails for this Sequoia and names no grades, and the clamp has to match your rail."),
 ("Does the 2023–2026 Toyota Sequoia have raised or flush roof rails?",
  "Both exist, and we could not confirm which grades get which. etrailer lists two roof types for the 2023 and 2024 Sequoia: \"Factory installed raised rails that run front to back\" and \"Flush mounted rails that run front to back\". It names no grades, and Toyota's releases for the 2023 reveal and the 2025 model year do not describe the roof rails at all. So check your own roof. Slide your fingers under the side rail between its end mounts. A gap you can pass a strap through means raised rails. A rail that sits tight to the roof along its whole length means flush rails. Raised-rail clamps and flush-rail feet are different parts, so settle this before you order anything."),
 ("What is the roof load limit on a 2023–2026 Sequoia?",
  "We could not confirm a Toyota roof figure from any page we could open, so the owner's manual is the authority. Read its roof-load section before you load bars or a platform. The numbers we did read are modest for a full-size SUV. Rave Offroad lists the TRD Pro factory roof rack at 132 lb when the weight is evenly distributed. Rack Warehouse rates the Thule Evo Raised Rail rack for the Sequoia at 165 lb. The Tuyoung bars on this page print 260 lb in their title, which is the seller's bar figure. Use the lowest of the manual, the rack and the bars, and count the rack's own weight against it."),
 ("Do the TRD Pro's factory roof rack and the other grades' rails take the same crossbars?",
  "No. Rave Offroad describes the TRD Pro rack as a factory option on the Sequoia TRD Pro that secures into the factory roof rails, 67.5 in long, 48 in wide at the back and 51 in at the front, with a 132 lb evenly distributed limit. It is a basket, not a pair of rails, so rail-clamp crossbars have nothing to grip once it is fitted. Toyota's releases we read do not describe this rack, so we could not confirm whether every TRD Pro carries it. If your TRD Pro has the basket, use its tie-down points or ask the seller whether a carrier clamps to its tubes. If it has plain rails, the bars on this page apply like any other grade."),
 ("Will Thule or Yakima crossbars fit the 2023–2026 Sequoia?",
  "On raised rails, yes, by Rack Warehouse's fit data. It sells the Thule Evo Raised Rail rack for the 2001–2025 Sequoia at $444.90 with a 165 lb rating, and Yakima's TimberLine FX for the same years at $599.90, both for factory raised side rails and both without splitting the generations. We found no Thule or Yakima kit for a flush-rail Sequoia at Rack Warehouse or on etrailer, whose 2023 and 2024 pages show only Front Runner platforms. We also found no Thule or Yakima Amazon listing that names the 2023 or later Sequoia, so neither is a pick here. If your rails are raised, order through a rack dealer and have them confirm the bar length for your model year."),
 ("Do 2008–2022 Sequoia roof racks fit the 2023–2026 Sequoia?",
  "Do not assume so. The third-generation Sequoia moved to the GA-F platform shared with the Tundra, with a new body and roof, and the Amazon listings on this page all name 2023 or later. Rack Warehouse's Thule and Yakima raised-rail pages cover 2001 through 2025 as one span, which says the clamps adapt to a range of rail shapes, not that the two roofs are the same. Rack Warehouse also lists separate Prinsu platforms for the 2008–2022 and the 2023–2026 Sequoia. Buy bars whose title names your year, and keep any used 2008–2022 rack out of the cart unless the seller confirms it by model year."),
 ("Are Sequoia crossbars the same as Tundra crossbars?",
  "No. The Sequoia and Tundra share the GA-F platform, and our fitment notes flag a different roof. A pickup cab has no long roof with side rails front to back, so Tundra listings are for a different part. The Front Runner Slimsport on this page is sold under its own Sequoia part number, KSTS003T, and every crossbar title here names the Sequoia. Buy by the Sequoia name and the year, not by the shared platform."),
 ("Which crossbars cover the 2025 and 2026 Sequoia?",
  "By title, the Tuyoung 260 lb bars, the ANTS PART bars, the Heavy-Duty bars, the cargo basket and crossbar kit and the rooftop platform all run 2023 through 2026. The Front Runner Slimsport is listed on Amazon as 2023-Current, though OK4WD lists the same kit for 2023–2024. The ALLMyHomy OE-style bars stop at 2024 in the title we read. Toyota's 2025 release added the 1794 grade and its 2026 release made power folding third-row seats standard; neither describes a roof change, but we could not confirm the rails are unchanged either. If your Sequoia is newer than the listing's last year, choose a listing that names your year or get the seller's answer in writing."),
 ("Do crossbars work with the Sequoia's panoramic moonroof?",
  "Toyota's 2025 release lists a standard panoramic moonroof on the Platinum and a panoramic roof on the 1794 grade. Crossbars sit on the side rails above the glass line, so the bars themselves are not the issue. What to check is the load: a cargo box's front edge, a basket's fairing or a bike's front wheel can sit over the glass. Front Runner says the Slimsport's fairing cutout keeps moonroof functionality on the Sequoia kit. For any set here, load the rack, then open the moonroof once while parked and watch what moves before you drive."),
 ("Should I buy crossbars, a basket or a full platform for a Sequoia?",
  "Buy for what you carry. Two bars take a cargo box, skis, a kayak or bikes and weigh the least, which matters on a roof whose published figures run 132 to 165 lb. A basket adds walls for loose gear and a place to strap a cooler, at the cost of noise and weight. A platform like the Front Runner Slimsport gives a flat 105 x 54.4 in deck with T-slots for light bars, tents and cases, but OK4WD lists it at 103.6 lb before you add anything, and etrailer says the factory rails come off to fit Front Runner's Sequoia platforms. For most families, bars first, then a cargo box; a platform suits owners building an overland rig."),
 ("Are the budget Amazon crossbars safe for a cargo box or kayak?",
  "They are sold for it, and every title here names the Sequoia and its years, but the proof is thinner than with Thule or Yakima. Only the Tuyoung title prints a rating, 260 lb, and says lockable. The ANTS PART, Heavy-Duty and ALLMyHomy titles print no rating. We could not open an amazon.com page to read clamp details or warranty terms, so compare the clamp in the listing photos with your rail, keep the total under the figure in your owner's manual, and recheck the clamps after the first week and after any long trip with a box on. For a box left on all year, the Thule or Yakima raised-rail kits from a rack dealer are the safer money."),
]

